lines=['# A modest bank of fixed geometric stress speeds','', 'Calibration: 27 October 2026. Audited and recorded: 28 October 2026. All 217 VIX quotes and all four maturities fitted jointly; SPX remains paused.','', f"Checking option loss is **{a['option_loss']:.6f}**, compared with **{b['option_loss']:.6f}** for the previously selected fitted two-speed model. Quotes inside bid–ask: **{a['inside_bidask']}/217**, versus {b['inside_bidask']}/217. Training loss is {t['option_loss']:.6f}. This compares two bounded fits on one stored market snapshot, not performance across market regimes.", '', 'The four-node bank is retained as an experimental candidate, not adopted as a reliable exact-forward calibration. Training forward means match, but their block SEs are much larger than the equality residuals, and checking errors reach 0.216 VIX points. The current numerical experiment does not establish an improvement over the two-speed model, or an inability of this bank family to fit the forwards. Improve forward estimation before increasing the bank further.', '', '## Choosing the half-lives','', 'We fixed the half-lives before calibration:', '', '$$h_j=7\\,4^{j-1}\\text{ days},\\qquad j=1,2,3,4,$$', '', '| Half-life | Calendar interpretation |', '|---:|---|', '| 7 days | One week |', '| 28 days | Four weeks, roughly one month |', '| 112 days | Sixteen weeks, roughly four months |', '| 448 days | Sixty-four weeks, roughly fifteen months |', '', 'Each step multiplies the persistence time by four. Equal spacing on a logarithmic axis covers short and persistent stress with only four nodes. These calendar scales were not selected to reproduce the earlier fitted 71/365-day pair. This is a transparent modelling choice, not a theorem that these endpoints are optimal.', '', 'The 7-day node can describe shocks that fade within the 30-day VIX averaging window. The 28/112-day nodes span intermediate persistence. The 448-day node allows stress to outlast the longest priced expiry and extends beyond the previous 365-day search ceiling. A half-life measures shock decay; it is not an option expiry. Every node affects all maturities.', '', 'Long half-lives can be difficult to distinguish over a short observation/pricing horizon, especially when sensitivities are also fitted. A fitted weight on a node therefore does not prove the market contains precisely that persistence. A later grid-sensitivity test would be separate; this experiment does not choose a new grid after viewing checking prices.', '', '## The shared variance process','', '$$dZ_t^j=-a_jZ_t^jdt+\\sqrt{2a_j}dB_t^j,\\quad Z_0^j=0,\\quad a_j=\\log2/h_j,$$', '', '$$A_t^j=\\exp\\left(b_jZ_t^j-\\tfrac12b_j^2(1-e^{-2a_jt})\\right),$$', '', '$$v_t=f+(\\xi(t)-f)\\left[\\alpha_0R_t+\\sum_{j=1}^4\\alpha_jA_t^j\\right],\\quad\\alpha_j\\ge0,\\quad\\sum_{j=0}^4\\alpha_j=1.$$', '', 'Here $R_t$ is the original normalized M2 response. The four stress Brownian motions are independent of each other and the old M2 bank, matching the independence assumption used in the previous two-speed test. Each response has mean one, so $E[v_t]=\\xi(t)$ and $v_t\\ge f$ when $\\xi(t)\\ge f$. Mixture weights apply to the normalized non-floor variance response, not to option prices.', '', 'Only speeds are fixed. Four sensitivities, four independent mixture weights, seven active variance levels and the floor are fitted: 16 parameters, versus 14 previously. Nine inactive curve levels remain unchanged. The amplitude bound is 5, active variance upper bound 0.2, floor volatility 5–12%. Positive weights use stick-breaking internally so every trial remains a positive mixture. There is no sparsity penalty or smoothness prior on the weights.', '', 'The old M2 dynamics, readout, positive spike shift, premiums and smooth cap remain frozen. Stress exponentials have their Gaussian normalization and no hard state cap. The bank is a finite positive measure over speeds; a continuous speed measure is not simultaneously calibrated.', '', '## Fitted bank','', '| Component | Sensitivity | Weight in normalized response |','|---|---:|---:|',f"| M2 | Frozen | {100*m['M2_weight']:.4f}% |"]
