lines+=['',f"Maximum training forward gap: {max(abs(np.array(t['forward_errors']))):.3g} VIX points. These are equalities on the calibration estimator. Checking residuals and SEs do not certify exact population forward matching.", '', f"Paired change in historical total loss (options plus checking-forward contribution): {pair['loss_change']:+.6f}; eight-block jackknife SE {pair['paired_jackknife_se']:.6f}. Shared old-state streams are reflected in the pairing. This uncertainty excludes fitting variability, grid uncertainty and model error.", '', 'Training forward block SEs range from about 0.049 to 0.154 VIX points; checking SEs range from 0.038 to 0.083. The checking gaps are roughly 2.5 checking SEs, and are smaller relative to combined training/checking uncertainty. This is a numerical reliability limitation rather than evidence that the model family cannot match the forwards.', '', '## Adding further half-lives', '', 'More finite nodes are mathematically admissible, but independent drivers can diversify away stress as their weights spread. A denser independent bank is not simply a finer quadrature of the same random continuous spectrum. For genuinely smooth refinement, correlated factors driven by a small number of common shocks are a possible separate comparison. See [the refinement note](STRESS_BANK_REFINEMENT.md). The present independent four-node model was kept unchanged during fitting.', '', '## Cached bank and numerical checks','', 'For European VIX prices we cache terminal standard-normal coordinates at each expiry and compute future conditional variance analytically. Complete joint time paths are not needed for these marginal prices. Speeds are fixed, while amplitudes and weights rebuild responses, variance integrals, VIX and payoffs. Reusing coordinates does not mean reusing completed prices.', '', 'Training reuses 32,768 old/node2/node3 coordinates per expiry from earlier work, and checking reuses 65,536. Nodes0/1 are newly drawn jointly from a defensive Gaussian mixture, independently permuted within each block. The target has four independent Gaussian stress coordinates. Product importance likelihoods are used without sample normalization. Checking is not wholly fresh and uses the same market snapshot.', '', 'The multilevel identity is $E[P_{bank}]=E[P_{reference}]+E[P_{bank}-P_{reference}]$. The reference replaces the first three stress responses by their unconditional mean one and retains the slowest node and M2. The large term uses original likelihoods; both paired terms use identical product likelihoods and controls. Both sides form conditional variance before the VIX square root. This changes the estimator, not the bank model.', '', 'All 16 derivative directions and the exact reference boundary replay pass. The independent audit reconstructs likelihoods, replays all 32 additional checking seeds, checks Gaussian mean-one normalization and conditional expectations with GH80, and reconstructs VIX on payoff-relevant states using adaptive scalar stress integrals. Existing M2 conditional tables and their earlier audits are reused. These numerical checks are not a new Lean theorem or uniform error certificate.', '', '| Days | Weighted tail payoff ESS | Top 10 tail share | Likelihood mass ± SE |','|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for z in audit['weighted_tails']:lines.append(f"| {z['day']} | {z['payoff_ESS']:.1f} | {100*z['top10_fraction']:.3f}% | {z['mass']:.6f} ± {z['mass_se']:.6f} |")
lines+=['',f"Negative native checking price estimates: bank {a['negative_native_prices']}; previous two-speed {b['negative_native_prices']}. They are preserved.", '', 'The joint SLSQP stage is preserved in runs/m2_stress_bank_001. A finishing least-squares step adjusts only the seven already-free variance levels at fixed stress parameters, restoring the four forward equalities for each candidate. Original and restored candidates are retained and selection uses training loss only. New additional checking coordinates are generated after this final selection. This changes optimization completion, not the variance model, grid, quote set or forward targets.', '', 'The two-speed reference is the earlier selected fit and stored checking blocks; it is not refitted here. The new fixed-speed family does not contain those exact fitted speeds, so the comparison is not a nested-model test. Three starts were attempted; all successes/failures and feasibility gaps are retained. Neither the production baseline nor the working VIX candidate is replaced.', '', '## Artifacts','', '- [Four smile panels](visualizations/stress-bank025/vix-stress-bank-smiles.png)', '- [Right wings](visualizations/stress-bank025/vix-stress-bank-right-wing.png)', '- [Call prices](visualizations/stress-bank025/vix-stress-bank-prices.png)', '- [Checking forwards](visualizations/stress-bank025/vix-stress-bank-forwards.png)', '- [Persistence grid and fitted weights](visualizations/stress-bank025/stress-bank-persistence-weights.png)', '- [Experiment plan](STRESS_BANK_PLAN.md)', '- Run: `runs/m2_stress_bank_002`.']
